# 高频词汇 List09
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List09核心词汇

{{solution}}{/səˈluːʃn/}{解决方案；溶液}{Finding a solution to the traffic problem will take time.}}
{{source}}{/sɔːs/}{来源；源头}{Renewable energy sources are becoming more affordable.}}
{{specific}}{/spəˈsɪfɪk/}{具体的；特定的}{The report highlights specific areas for improvement.}}
{{stable}}{/ˈsteɪbl/}{稳定的；马厩}{The patient's condition is now stable.}}
{{status}}{/ˈsteɪtəs/}{地位；状态}{The status of the negotiations is still unclear.}}
{{stimulate}}{/ˈstɪmjuleɪt/}{刺激；激发}{The tax cut was designed to stimulate economic activity.}}
{{strategy}}{/ˈstrætədʒi/}{策略；战略}{The long-term strategy focuses on innovation and growth.}}
{{stress}}{/stres/}{压力；强调}{The report stresses the importance of early intervention.}}
{{structure}}{/ˈstrʌktʃər/}{结构；构造}{The essay has a clear and logical structure.}}
{{submit}}{/səbˈmɪt/}{提交；服从}{All proposals must be submitted by the end of the month.}}
{{subsequent}}{/ˈsʌbsɪkwənt/}{随后的；后来的}{Subsequent research confirmed the original findings.}}
{{substantial}}{/səbˈstænʃl/}{大量的；实质的}{The company made a substantial profit last year.}}
{{sufficient}}{/səˈfɪʃnt/}{足够的；充分的}{There is sufficient evidence to proceed with the case.}}
{{summarize}}{/ˈsʌməraɪz/}{总结；概括}{The report summarizes the key findings of the study.}}
{{survey}}{/ˈsɜːveɪ/}{调查；测量}{A recent survey found that 70% of employees prefer remote work.}}
{{survive}}{/səˈvaɪv/}{幸存；存活}{The company survived the financial crisis by cutting costs.}}
{{sustain}}{/səˈsteɪn/}{维持；支撑}{It is difficult to sustain growth without investment in education.}}
{{target}}{/ˈtɑːɡɪt/}{目标；靶子}{The campaign targets young adults aged 18 to 25.}}
{{technique}}{/tekˈniːk/}{技术；技巧}{The artist used a unique technique to create the painting.}}
{{temporary}}{/ˈtemprəri/}{临时的；暂时的}{The arrangement is temporary until a permanent solution is found.}}
{{tendency}}{/ˈtendənsi/}{趋势；倾向}{There is a tendency for people to resist change.}}
{{theory}}{/ˈθɪəri/}{理论；学说}{The theory was supported by experimental data.}}
{{threat}}{/θret/}{威胁；恐叫}{Cybersecurity threats are a growing concern for businesses.}}
{{tolerate}}{/ˈtɒləreɪt/}{容忍；忍受}{The system cannot tolerate any further delays.}}
{{tradition}}{/trəˈdɪʃn/}{传统；惯例}{The tradition of giving gifts during holidays dates back centuries.}}
{{transform}}{/trænsˈfɔːm/}{转变；改造}{Technology has the power to transform entire industries.}}
{{trend}}{/trend/}{趋势；潮流}{The trend toward sustainable living is growing globally.}}
{{trigger}}{/ˈtrɪɡər/}{触发；引发}{The announcement triggered a surge in stock prices.}}
{{ultimate}}{/ˈʌltɪmət/}{最终的；极限的}{The ultimate aim is to achieve universal literacy.}}
{{undergo}}{/ˌʌndəˈɡəʊ/}{经历；经受}{The system underwent a major upgrade last year.}}
